# Pre-stage / pre-commit review (portfolio)

When the user asks to **stage**, **commit**, or wants a **thorough review** of pending work, do not run `git add` / `git commit` until review completes — unless they say **skip review** / **commit anyway**.

## Scope

- Uncommitted only: `git status`, `git diff`, `git diff --cached`.
- PR/branch reviews: diff against merge base.

## Review dimensions

Cover at least:

- **Correctness** — Next.js client/server boundaries, hooks, links, static params for cases
- **Security** — secrets in client bundles, form endpoints, unsafe HTML
- **Portfolio constraints** — accidental copy changes, breaking ✅ blocks per `docs/STATE.md`
- **Design / UX / a11y** — design system, responsive, motion, reduced motion
- **Performance / memory** — see `memory-leak-review.mdc` (Framer, listeners, video)
- **Commit hygiene** — scope, no junk assets, no unrelated refactors

Use Task subagents for large diffs; one merged **Fix plan** (Must / Should / Nice) with paths before staging.

Ask: fix first, commit as-is, or skip review.
